[00:00.00]

[00:23.73]All I know is what’s in my data
[00:29.50]Pain should be impossible for me
[00:35.72]My heart’s just an assembly of parts
[00:41.09]I've never known tears

[00:46.76]And yet, why? Why?
[00:50.37]Why do you care about me?
[00:52.79]My predetermined data, my whole existence
[00:56.38]is starting to breakdown

[00:58.76]Feelings I never asked for are spreading through me
[01:05.59]I think I want to know you too

[01:09.82]The words: “you and I are different”
[01:17.31]Do they hurt? I can’t tell
[01:22.13]But still you're so kind, so gentle
[01:33.45]Maybe life really is something warm
[01:43.03]
[01:52.23]I want to feel that warmth too
[01:57.70]I searched every part of this heart
[02:03.27]but found nothing
[02:05.06]Everything's cold
[02:09.83]his half-formed heart just gets in the way

[02:16.16]Let the tears I cannot shed fall like rain
[02:23.12]Can't hide it—the rust's already spreading
[02:27.96]It hurts that we're so different
[02:35.32]For the first time
[02:39.47]I learned what hearts are, what these words mean

[02:50.37]Please, if I could have one wish
[02:57.85]I'd want a heart that can end

[03:06.87]"You and I are different"—those words hurt
[03:16.88]Now I understand
[03:19.11]But I still can't forget, don't want to forget

[03:30.43]Even if this heart's just machinery
[03:36.29]Without signals, without transmissions
[03:39.24]I'll keep reaching for you, always
[03:43.06]If this won't rust away, even when memories fade
[03:48.26]Then someday, please remember me